  "worked_solution": "We rewrite our integral and integrate term by term to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5{x}^{2}+6}{{x}^{2}(2x+3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{4}{3x}+\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{23}{3(2x+3)})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{23}{3}\\int \\frac{1}{2x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|x|-\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{23}{6}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|2x+3|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
